the managing partner or the affiliate of the managing partner on advances made by the managing
partner or such affiliate to a partnership will be at a rate not in excess of the lesser of the
effective rate then being paid by the managing partner or the affiliate for similar type borrowings
or the highest lawful rate, and in no event at a rate in excess of the amount which would be
charged to the partnership by independent third parties for the same purpose. The managing partner
or an affiliate of the managing partner may not receive points or other financing charges or fees
on advances made by it to a partnership. In addition, a partnership may not make loans to the
managing partner or any affiliate of the managing partner. The managing partner may pledge its
interest in a partnership but may not pledge partnership assets for its own benefit. The managing
partner however, may pledge its directly owned interest in drilling program properties at any time
and may sell its working interests in drilling program properties pursuant to the drilling program
