<DIV align="left" style="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 6pt">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;All or a portion of any gain recognized on the disposition of a depletable property or of
interests may be taxed as ordinary income to the extent of recapture of depletion deductions,
except for percentage depletion deductions in excess of the basis of the property. See &#147;&#151; Special
Features of Oil and Gas Taxation &#151; Sale of Property&#148; and &#147;&#151; Special Features of Oil and Gas
